  "explanation": "At $x = \\ln 2$: $y = \\frac{1}{2} + 2\\ln 2$ and $\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = 2 - \\mathrm{e}^{-x} = 2 - \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{3}{2}$. Tangent: $y - (\\frac{1}{2} + 2\\ln 2) = \\frac{3}{2}(x - \\ln 2)$. At $x = 0$: $c = \\frac{1}{2} + 2\\ln 2 - \\frac{3}{2}\\ln 2 = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}\\ln 2 \\approx 0.847$.",
  "workedSolution": "1. At $x = \\ln 2$: $y = \\frac{1}{2} + 2\\ln 2$ and $\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = 2 - \\mathrm{e}^{-x} = 2 - \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{3}{2}$. Tangent: $y - (\\frac{1}{2} + 2\\ln 2) = \\frac{3}{2}(x - \\ln 2)$. At $x = 0$: $c = \\frac{1}{2} + 2\\ln 2 - \\frac{3}{2}\\ln 2 = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}\\ln 2 \\approx 0.847$.",
